etoro-watchlists-response.json

# Immutable local broker evidence
data/evidence/

# iCloud Drive sync conflict copies ("reasoning_service 2.py"). The second
# rule covers a tenth conflict onwards ("... 10.json"), which the first
# cannot match — it matters because data/knowledge/ is tracked and receives
# generated files. Check additions with `git check-ignore`, not by eye.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9][0-9].*

# Cached provider evidence — re-fetchable, never source of truth
data/cache/

# data/knowledge/ is deliberately NOT ignored. A knowledge entry is not
# rebuildable byte-identically — two grounded readings of one immutable
# filing may quote different spans — so it fails the technical definition
# of a cache, and Git is what records which reading schema produced it.
# The decision, its reassessment criteria and the conditions under which
# this would change are in docs/PROJECT_STATE.md.

# The Artificial CIO's decision journal. Written every cycle, and the
# memory it feeds belongs to the machine that made those decisions — a
# fresh clone has no history and honestly says so rather than replaying
# someone else's. Tracking it also put this directory in the path of
# iCloud's conflict copies, twice.
data/events/

# The investor's decision ledger — durable operational state, never cache
# and never corpus. Company knowledge is grounded against public immutable
# sources and serves engineering; a decision event records the investor's
# actual portfolio and policy context at a moment, belongs to their
# operational history, and is not re-derivable. It stays out of version
# control (back it up like data, not like code); tests carry synthetic
# decision events only.
data/decisions/

# Claude Code: shared project settings are tracked; personal overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
